Fig. 6 The specificity of the aptasensor detection of LPS $\mathrm{{(1.0\ng/mL)}}$ in $\mathrm{pH}7.5$ Tris-HCl detection buffer against the interface substances: HSA ( $10~\mathrm{{ng/mL}}$ ); PCT ( $10~\mathrm{{ng/mL}}$ ) and CRP ( $10~\mathrm{{ng/mL}}$ ).
The long-term stability experiment was investigated by storing the proposed electrode at $4^{\circ}\mathrm{C}$ and measuring every week. No obvious change was found in the first week, and the value of the ratio $(I_{\mathrm{Cu-MOFs}}/I_{\mathrm{Fc}})$ changed less than $0.78\%$ of the initial value of the ratio $(I_{\mathrm{Cu-MOFs}}/I_{\mathrm{Fc}})$ . After a longer storage for three weeks, the value maintained $97.5\%$ of the initial value. The results illustrated that the prepared aptasensor exhibited satisfactory stability.
Four prepared electrodes with incubating the same LPS concentration $(10\:\mathrm{pg/mL)}$ were used to investigate the reproducibility of the aptasensor under the same conditions. Close values of the ratio $(I_{\mathrm{Cu-MOFs}}/I_{\mathrm{Fc}})$ with a relative standard deviation (RSD) of $0.29\%$ $(n~=~4)$ ) were obtained with the four electrodes, suggesting an acceptable reproducibility of the aptasensor.
## CONCLUSIONS
In conclusion, an electrochemical aptasensor for ratiometric electrochemical detection of LPS was reported based on Cu-MOFs as a catalyst and target-triggered quadratic cycles for signal amplification in this study. With the help of phi29 and N.BstNBI, quadratic cycles were carried out for achieving a large number of capture probes, which could make the original signal molecules of Fc decrease, and then HP3/AuNPs/Cu-MOFs signal probes were hybridized with capture probes to obtain the enhanced catalysis response of Cu-MOFs. The peak currents ratio of the CuMOFs and Fc was measured for ratiometric electrochemical detection of LPS. In this work, the AuNPs/Cu-MOFs are not only used as nanocarriers to immobilize HP3 and as electroactive materials for signal report, but also acted as a catalyst to oxide glucose for enzyme-free signal amplification. Compared to common electrochemical
## Analytical Chemistry
detection method, the ratiometric electrochemical assay provides advantages of decrease of difference between batches and improvement of accuracy and sensitivity. Thus, we anticipate that this principle might open up new opportunities for other analytes detection.
